    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d285">

                <pb facs="0401" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3295</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Belden</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-09T00:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 9, 1917, midnight</hi></date>. <lb/>
                            [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 10, 5 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram February 3, 1 p.m. Colombian Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    to-day acknowledged note without reference to similar action. Commercial
                    interests anxious. Some apprehension exists as to invasion of Colombian
                    territory by the United States to protect canal if there is war. Germans here
                    will agitate this issue. <pb facs="0402" n="230" xml:id="pg230"/> I believe
                    therefore that the approval of Colombian treaty at this time would be
                    advantageous. See my telegram of February 3, 11 a.m.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d285-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I have urged consuls to watch Germans.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Belden</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
